WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.760
Charles?! What are you doing here?

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:13.300
I came in pursuit of you, Princess Teresa de
Larsenburg, future queen of Larsenburg.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.510
Just kidding!

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:24.590
My university is on holiday, so I wanted
to see your beloved Japan, Teresa.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.510
What about work?

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:31.300
As long as I have my computer and smartphone,
I can do general tasks, no matter where I go.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.300
These flowers are so pretty.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.380
They're the "Teresa, Princess of Larsenburg,"
which I had made recently.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.800
It means "vow of love" in the language of flowers.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.510
Lovely, isn't it?

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.380
"Vow of love"...

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.340
Thank you, Charles.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.800
You'd like to tour our high school?

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:55.260
You can introduce me as just your childhood friend.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.550
Telling your friends the truth would
cause a lot of trouble, right?

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.880
Understood. I'll make arrangements for your tour.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.050
Thank you.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:04.840
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.670
Isn't that great, Miss Teresa?

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.380
What?

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:21.050
I feel reassured about everything
since Sir Charles came for you.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.630
You like Charles, right?

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.920
I do.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:36.470
Because I respect him, and he is a fine fiancé worthy
of you, Teresa, the future queen of Larsenburg.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.010
That's true...

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:50.550
Tada Never Falls in Love

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.050
Chotto matte kocchi muite

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.470
Finder wa itsumo kimatte

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.880
Kimi ja nai to pin to konai

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.050
Boku wa douka shichatta no kai?

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.380
"O-tomodachi" o toorikoshite

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.510
Surechigai no koibito-miman mo

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:13.010
Sore wa souzoushii sekai

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.380
Ki ga tsukeba, marude niji no you sa

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.800
Kisetsu yo tomare

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.920
Kimi to kiritotta jikan ga, shashin no naka de

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:32.300
Are mo kore mo sore mo dore mo kagayaiten da yo

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:38.380
Nee kimi ni, kimi ni hitotsu tsutaetokitain da

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:45.470
Mou tomaranai, kakushi kirenai, omoi ga koko ni an da yo

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:53.720
Baby, omoide to iu film no naka e kimi ga tokete shimau mae ni

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.470
Todoketai kotoba ga an da yo

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.220
"Ima kimi ni koi shiteru yo"

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.920
I'm Not a Rain-bringer

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.130
Photo Contest

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.130
Come Join the
Photography Club!!

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.420
Wh-wh-who...

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.420
Who is that dashing man who seems as if he's been
blessed by God with the whole package, Tada?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.220
I don't know.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.840
Well, he's no match for me, right?!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.840
This is Charles, my childhood friend.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.420
His university is out for summer break,
so he came to visit Japan.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.470
Bonjour! I'm Charles de Loire. It's a pleasure.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.760
All of these photos are so lovely.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.550
Right?

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.720
They taught me how to take pictures, you know.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.050
That sounds like fun.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.720
These are...

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.590
I took those pictures.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.550
Wh-what?!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:05.090
I see! You look cool in your photos,
but you look far cooler in person, Ijuin-kun!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:11.720
I know, right?! Photos don't do my charm justice!
You get that, don't you, Charles?!

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:09.720
Yeah.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.880
Ijuin-senpai drastically changes at the drop of a hat
when he gets a compliment.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.090
Indeed.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.340
These animals have some nice expressions, too.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.840
I took those pictures.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.970
I can feel the effort the photographer put into it.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.760
Oh, Charles-san! You get me!
I'm so happy! Thanks, man!

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.380
You, too?!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.130
These are very beautiful scenic photos.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.550
Of course. Those are the places where HINA
did her gravure photoshoots...

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.800
in other words...

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.010
holy places, that's why!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.300
HINA?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.420
That is his favorite gravure idol.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.380
Huh...? She's...

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.220
What's so funny?

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:05.470
My apologies. She certainly is beautiful like a goddess.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:12.590
Just as I'd expect from Teresa-kun's childhood friend!
He has a good eye! He is an extremely fine gentleman!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.760
These are pretty flowers and birds.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.920
Those are Hasegawa-san's photos!

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.380
They're lovely, mademoiselle.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.880
Thank you very much.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.760
And these?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.760
Those photos are mine.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.510
I see... Tada-kun's photos...

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:37.470
They're marvelous! I feel like I understand the beauty
of Japan just by looking at these photos!

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.380
Thank you very much.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.880
So, where is your photo, Teresa?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.470
This one is mine!

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:45.670
A rock?

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.630
It looked like a penguin smiling. Isn't it cute?

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.090
This is a courting penguin, right?

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.590
Yes! I found it in the courtyard!

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:55.970
Excellent. You two are attuned to each other.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.050
So, they can tell it's a penguin.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.130
Then, this photo is yours, right, Alec?

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:05.720
You're always good at finding adorable things, after all.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.010
I-is that so?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.170
It's a very nice photo!

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.050
Oh? Are you blushing, Alec?!

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.010
Eep!

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.380
Oh, and your photo, too, Teresa!

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.590
Do you really think so?

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.800
Of course! I mean it!

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:20.720
Geez...

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.720
Oh! Please look at the picture I took the other day!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:28.720
Don't Charles and Teresa-chan
look somewhat alike, Mitsuyoshi?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.380
Alec won, you know!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.720
Really? They're all lovely!

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.920
Yeah, they do.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:32.840
Right?

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:36.220
Tada Coffee Shop

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.260
Here! Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.880
Mm, it's delicious!

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:41.550
Thank you very much.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:45.010
It's nice that you have such a lovely shop next door.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:47.130
If I were you, I'd wind up visiting every day.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:50.260
Please visit! We'd be delighted to have you!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.340
Thank you, Yui-san. I'll definitely drop
by when I'm in the area.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:55.260
Okay!

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.380
Wow! They're sparkling!

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.880
Is Charles-san really just your childhood friend?

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:03.920
Yes, he is.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.340
Oh, yeah?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.670
Oh? Was this your seat?

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.590
What's your name?

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:14.470
WHA-?!

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.800
His name is Nyanko Big.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.970
Meow!

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.550
Nyanko Big, huh?

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:22.010
That's a unique name. It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.420
Purr, purr, purr...

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.510
An intrepid Nyanko Big.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.300
Huh?

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.050
He acts totally different when it's me!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.550
No fair, Nyanko Big! Be nice to me, too!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.670
Hiss!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.420
Eek!

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.800
And while we're at it, a trepid Nyanko Big.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:44.090
There are plenty of lovely photos here, too...

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:50.760
Amazing people really do exist!

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:54.420
He's cool, kind, and Nyanko Big even likes him!

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.920
He also manages a company while attending university.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.760
He's superman, then!

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:00.720
Yes, he is.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.630
Hmph! Well, I'm gonna be a big
and super chef some day!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.970
Right, Mitsuyoshi?!

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:07.800
Good luck.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.670
Thanks!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.300
Is this also Tada-kun's photo?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.630
Huh? Oh... no.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.170
That photo was taken by my late father.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:26.760
Tada-kun and Yui-chan's father was a photographer.
He and their mother died in an accident ten years ago.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.090
I see...

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:34.170
It must've been difficult for you since they both passed.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.340
I've got Grandpa, Big Bro, and Nyanko Big, so it's okay!

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.220
Yeah!

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.970
It seems that way.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:45.220
Tada Coffee Shop

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.260
I really enjoyed today.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:46.970
Please come by again.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.010
Charles-san, you're going to be
in Japan for a while, right?

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:50.630
Yeah!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:56.220
Oh! Well, you know, there's a party tomorrow,
so why don't you guys come, Charles included?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.470
I'm a celebrity, so I'll invite you to a celebrity party!

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:05.220
Kaoru-kun, I believe real celebs
don't call themselves celebrities.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.090
For real?!

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:11.380
Thank you for the invitation, Ijuin-kun. But I'm
afraid I have a previous engagement tomorrow.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.510
I see. Then, what about Teresa-chan and Alec?

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.670
We have plans, too.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.880
Really? That's a shame...

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.260
Well, you're going, right, Mitsuyoshi?!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.670
The party's gonna be like, "Ta-da! Free food,"
but not like, "Tada, here's your food."

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.340
Hey, give me something!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:29.170
Well, we'll take our leave.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.050
Thank you for the coffee!

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.090
See ya later, Teresa-chan and Alec!

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.840
Good night!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.880
I want to see Nyanko Big again!

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.590
He's cute, isn't he?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.010
Charles-san seems like a real prince!

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:47.920
Well, he's no match for me!

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.510
That means Big Bro can't win against him...

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.380
What are you talking about?

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.130
Hey, over here!

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.010
This way, guys!

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.130
I-is it okay for us to be at a party like this, Tada?

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.470
Probably... yeah.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.380
Is my bow tie okay like this?

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.470
It's fine.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.550
Hey! It's a good thing you came looking
like some Japanese innkeeper.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.550
Youch!

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:33.760
Sheesh...

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:37.220
This is seriously like, a legit celebrity party, huh?

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.800
There's a lot of meat over there, Yamashita.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.630
For reals?! Awesome!

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:44.300
Let's get going!

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.170
Wait, what?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.840
Isn't that Charles-san?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.670
Huh? Where? Where?

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.170
Look, way over there.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.970
Whoa! You're right!

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.420
Who are the ladies who are with him?

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.840
Aren't they his girlfriends?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.170
What?! Two girlfriends?!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.260
How insolent! He's much too popular! Right, Tada?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.170
No, they're...

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:12.840
T-T-T-Teresa-chan and A-A-Alec-Alec?!

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.130
They're so beautiful!

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:14.970
Yeah!

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.920
Are you serious?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.920
Wait, what are they doing here?!

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.170
Tada-kun?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:37.670
Hey!

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.970
Fancy meeting all of you here!

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.720
Charles!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.970
What are the odds of us planning
to attend the same party?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.550
Yeah! I'm seriously shocked!
And Teresa-chan and Alec were with you, huh?

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:53.510
An acquaintance of mine threw this party,
so I invited these two to come along.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.380
Oh, so that's why.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:00.720
Man, you two are super pretty!
We're super impressed! Right, Mitsuyoshi?

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.090
Hey, you're staring.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.090
Oh, sorry.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.590
Monsieur Loire!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.260
Shall we finish saying hello?

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:16.300
Sure.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.420
We'll see you later.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.630
Later.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.880
See ya!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:24.260
Wow... He really is a bona fide celebrity.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.010
Hmph! Of course!

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.840
Well, I guess I'll go say hello!

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.380
I was talking about Charles-san...

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.630
I smell roast beef!

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.720
That's Yamashita Dog for you.
I'm surprised he could tell.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.880
I'll say hello, too!

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.970
Hold it right there, Hajime-chan.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.010
Guess I'll go take some pictures or something...

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:58.970
What do you think of summer in Japan, Monsieur Loire?

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:04.510
I had heard from a friend that it's hotter than Africa
here, but I never expected that that would be true.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:06.920
Is that so?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.010
Well, summer will be at its peak from here on out.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.630
Oh! I'm so sorry!

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.170
No, it's my fault!

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:13.970
My, what should we do about that?

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:16.590
Let's get you in another dress right away.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.920
No, it'll be okay if I wipe it off.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:19.800
But...

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.550
Really, it's okay...

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.800
I'm truly sorry.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:26.630
That sounds like fun!

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.760
Yeah. Please come with us next time.

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.670
Let Charles know.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:32.170
Okay.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:38.170
There!

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.220
That...!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:51.380
That looks like the building that appeared in the
final episode of Rainbow Shogun season one!

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:56.220
Wow...

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.170
It'll only be for a bit...

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.880
Alec, shall we dance?

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.800
No, I...

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:20.630
Please, at least until Teresa comes back.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.220
I wonder who he's going to dance with.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.130
Me!

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:24.920
Me!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.220
Me, for sure!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.720
Okay...

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:37.800
Wow!

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:37.800
My...!

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.220
How lovely!

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.970
I'm so jealous!

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.130
I wonder what their relationship is.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:49.550
If you make such a scary face, I'll feel like I bullied you
into this. So, could you smile a little for me?

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.300
I see...

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.970
Looks like it's going to rain.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:08.510
Guess I'll head back in.

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:14.920
Huh? Tada-kun?!

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.380
This way!

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:33.880
Are you okay?

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.670
Y-yeah...

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.630
You'll catch a cold...

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.510
Thank you very much.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.760
We've been through something like this before.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.420
Huh?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.840
Back when we first met.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:04.720
Where are you headed?

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.720
Huh?

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.470
I'll walk you home.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.420
Uh...

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:18.510
Now that you mention it... it was raining like this,
and you helped me out back then, too, Tada-kun.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:21.220
You really ARE Rainbow Sho-

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:22.590
I'm not a rain-bringer.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:23.590
Huh?

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:25.470
Oh, perhaps you're the rain-bringer?

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:26.970
N-no!

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:32.220
Oh, but when I was child, it always rained
on the days that we had picnics, I think?

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:33.670
That settles it.

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.510
What? So, it's me?

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:46.470
I'm glad all of Teresa's school friends are nice people.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:51.590
Is that so? Well, I don't know about some of them,
but for the most part, they are...

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:53.260
Achoo! Brrr... It's chilly!

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.220
Honestly, I was worried that she was getting homesick.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.220
I'm glad that my concern was unfounded.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.760
But being apart from each other is one thing.
Mutual neglect is another.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:15.260
Yeah...

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.420
That's from the recent Star Festival, right?

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.340
Yeah.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:24.470
Wow! So cute! He looks comfortable!

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:28.340
Nyanko Big-san is so gallant.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:33.630
When his tail is standing up straight,
it's proof that he's aware of the camera.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:34.840
Is that so?

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:45.720
Teresa sure is taking a while.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.630
I can't find her!

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.010
Where could she have gone?!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:01.050
Calm down a bit, Alec. She's an adult now.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:02.260
Right...

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.420
I'll go look for her now.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:08.130
Hm?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.340
Alec?

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:11.380
What's wrong?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.340
Teresa is gone!

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:17.340
It stopped raining.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.340
Yeah.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:26.050
It's the North Star. It's a lucky sign
that always shows us the way.

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:27.130
Huh?

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:30.760
My favorite nanny told me that.

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:32.420
Nanny?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:39.050
Uh... my parents were busy,
so I spent a lot of time with my nanny.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:46.130
No matter when or where you go,
the starlight guides you when you've lost your way.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:52.970
That's why, whenever I'm lost, I look up at the stars.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.630
Grandpa said the same thing.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.220
Really?

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:05.220
He said that the North Star always shows us the way.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.340
That's why I look up at the stars, too...

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.420
We've been looking at the same star, huh?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:21.970
Teresa!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:25.970
Alec?

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.010
I was worried about you, Teresa!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.260
I'm sorry...

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.300
I wanted to see this building...

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.720
but then, it rained...

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.840
so we took shelter from the rain.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.170
No, it's my fault.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.590
I let you go alone.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.800
Now, now, Alec.

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:12.050
Charles...

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:13.550
We've found her.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.470
Are you all right?

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:18.470
Yes...

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.670
Thanks, Tada-kun.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:25.170
No, I'm sorry. It's because I suggested
that we take shelter from the rain.

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:28.260
It's okay. I'm glad that you're both safe and sound.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.220
Well, shall we go, Teresa?

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.720
Alec, sorry about today...

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:06.720
I'm making soup right now, so...

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:12.590
I'll be careful from now on.

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:22.170
Tada-kun, Ijuin-kun, Hasegawa-san,
Pin-senpai, and Yamashita-kun...

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:26.010
They're all nice and wonderful friends
that I made in Japan.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:27.340
But...

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.510
once our study abroad is over,
we're going back to our country.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:33.510
And I'll marry Charles and become queen.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:37.880
I had made up my mind about that
when I came to Japan.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:42.010
Right.

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:12.470
Itsumademo tsuzuite yuku to, boku wa zutto omottetan da yo

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:23.720
Ano hi kimi ga kirei sugiru wake o, boku wa nani mo shiranakatta

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:29.970
Kamisama tte hito ga kimi o tsuresatte

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:35.920
Ni-do to wa aenai to boku ni iu

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:41.550
Doko ni ikun da yo, boku wa nani mo dekinakatta yo

00:22:41.550 --> 00:22:46.590
Utsukushi sugita hito yo

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:53.050
Aitakute, aitakute donna kimi demo

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:58.670
Negaigoto ga moshi hitotsu kanau naraba

00:22:59.050 --> 00:23:04.630
Imasugu ni, imasugu ni dakishimetain da yo

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:10.260
Zutto kimi no soba ni dake itakattan da

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:15.420
Kokoro no naka wa namida no ame no melody

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:24.130
Kimi to sugoshita hibi wa wasureru nante dekinain da yo

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.510
Yui-chan, where's Tada-senpai?

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:30.010
He said he'll be home soon!

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:34.260
Then, I'll play with Nyanko Big and wait.
I don't mind if he hisses at me!

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.880
No, you should mind...

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.880
Next time: Episode 7, "It's Better Than Crying"

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:40.880
It's Better Than Crying

00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:40.130
Please look forward to it!
